re/13993940/state.json" "file_sha256" "347b635e60b4f5225ccb2ca1aedb03aa9b77bacb38e05dde3b89bfde4f088cb9"} {"question" "q-279512" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/state.json" "file_sha256" "347b635e60b4f5225ccb2ca1aedb03aa9b77bacb38e05dde3b89bfde4f088cb9"} {"question" "q-279493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ If $f(X)={X}^{2}+1$, find $f(A).$\n\n| $f(A)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/state.json" "file_sha256" "347b635e60b4f5225ccb2ca1aedb03aa9b77bacb38e05dde3b89bfde4f088cb9"} {"question" "q-279493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}+I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}+I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+1 & 0+0 \\\\ 0+0 & -1+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/state.json" "file_sha256" "347b635e60b4f5225ccb2ca1aedb03aa9b77bacb38e05dde3b89bfde4f088cb9"} {"question" "q-279493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5f9d41fb3d6ea0c003801a20c8806967f2b03a19ae29030a1297e1301428f2c6"} {"question" "q-279493" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/state.json" "file_sha256" "347b635e60b4f5225ccb2ca1aedb03aa9b77bacb38e05dde3b89bfde4f088cb9"} {"question" "q-279493" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/state.json" "file_sha256" "347b635e60b4f5225ccb2ca1aedb03aa9b77bacb38e05dde3b89bfde4f088cb9"} {"question" "q-279493" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/state.json" "file_sha256" "347b635e60b4f5225ccb2ca1aedb03aa9b77bacb38e05dde3b89bfde4f088cb9"} {"question" "q-279493" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/state.json" "file_sha256" "347b635e60b4f5225ccb2ca1aedb03aa9b77bacb38e05dde3b89bfde4f088cb9"} {"question" "q-279493" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/state.json" "file_sha256" "347b635e60b4f5225ccb2ca1aedb03aa9b77bacb38e05dde3b89bfde4f088cb9"}